libnfs 8.0.0: a failed NFSv3 open returns the real errno, not -EIO.

nfs3_open_create_cb() and nfs3_open_cb() pass an err that is already a
negative errno through nfsstat3_to_errno() again, which maps every value it
does not know to -EIO. So ENOENT, EACCES, ENOTDIR, ESTALE and the rest from a
failed open all reach the caller as -EIO. This is a backport of upstream
master, which passes err through unchanged. libnfs 8.0.0 (pinned here) has the
same code as 6.0.2; the hunks below are B2's with 8.0.0 line numbers.

Origin: Mediahro lane B2, mediahro PR #21 at a494b58,
packages/mediahro_ffi/test/network/patches/libnfs-6.0.2-open-errno.patch.

Licence: this is a modification of libnfs, which is LGPL-2.1-or-later, and the
change is under the same licence. The modified source is offered with the
release's mediahro-deps-sources.tar, which carries this patch next to the
pinned upstream tarball (LGPL-2.1 section 6).

Applied by scripts/sources.py with patch -p1 from the libnfs-8.0.0 root, on
every platform.

--- a/lib/nfs_v3.c
+++ b/lib/nfs_v3.c
@@ -4906,7 +4906,7 @@
 	struct open_cb_data *cb_data = private_data;
 
         if (err) {
-		cb_data->cb(nfsstat3_to_errno(err), nfs,
+		cb_data->cb(err, nfs,
                          nfs_get_error(nfs), cb_data->private_data);
                 free_open_cb_data(cb_data);
                 return;
@@ -5066,7 +5066,7 @@
                 return;
         }
         if (err) {
-                cb_data->cb(nfsstat3_to_errno(err), nfs,
+                cb_data->cb(err, nfs,
                             nfs_get_error(nfs), cb_data->private_data);
                 free_open_cb_data(cb_data);
                 return;
